Include <crypt.h> for crypt().

crypt() is reached through <unistd.h>, which declares it only as a leftover
from when it was part of the C library. glibc's own header says so and tells
callers to include <crypt.h> instead; llvm-libc does not declare it at all,
since libxcrypt is what provides it.

--- a/pam_passwdqc.c
+++ b/pam_passwdqc.c
@@ -14,6 +14,7 @@
 #include <limits.h>
 #include <unistd.h>
 #include <pwd.h>
+#include <crypt.h>
 #ifdef HAVE_SHADOW
 #include <shadow.h>
 #endif
